From 11eae2099181fd39c776a7791fe9624ccef3642c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 11:09:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Gateway tick passes read once per pass, not once per
 card

Hub gateway profile 2026-11-12 (t_01a1ccca7a1979a7; 4,948 cards, 139% of a core after PR1170/PR1125):
- divergence repair: one replica read per 500 settled cards and one omissions read per pass
  (was one SELECT of each per card every sync round, 13% of samples)
- tui owner claim: one owned_live_session answer per chat per collector tick
  (was one state.db lineage walk per pending row, 1,655 rows over 122 chats, 9%)
- wait notices: the already-posted check runs before the queue place (5%)
- gateway_names: answer reused while hub.db, its WAL and the mail config keep identity/size/mtime,
  5 s at most, never for a file written inside the timestamp granularity (4%)

No pass, notice or retry is removed; each change has an operation-budget test that failed before it.
